  "text": "Why is Redis 100 times faster than MySQL? Here's the secret. RAM access takes 100 nanoseconds, but disk I/O takes 100 microseconds! That is a 1,000x hardware gap. Plus, Redis runs on a single-threaded event loop with zero lock contention. Never replace MySQL with Redis. Use Redis as a cache buffer, and keep MySQL as your database! Follow StackShade for daily engineering breakdowns.",
